    "body": "Adds ADR-018, which decides to implement three state pseudo-classes (`:link`, `:visited`, `:hover`). ADR-008 deferred pseudo-classes to a future ADR; this is that ADR, scoped to the most visible gap.\n\n## The gap this fixes\n\nAs of v0.4.0, every `<a>` renders identically regardless of whether the user visited it or is hovering over it. Firefox and Chrome have shipped visited-link purple and hover feedback since the mid-1990s. That's the most visible remaining gap in the selector layer.\n\n## Architectural decision\n\n**State lives outside the DOM.**\n\n    dom::Document (immutable after parse)\n        |\n        v\n    RenderState (mutable, owned by RenderPipeline)\n        visited_urls, hovered_element, pointer_x/y\n        |\n        v\n    cascade(doc, styles, state) -> ComputedStyleMap\n\n`dom::Element` does not grow state fields. ADR-007's \"DOM is data\" invariant stays intact.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `RenderState` struct in `css/cascade.hpp`\n- `Selector::matches(node, state)` overload; existing single-arg overload delegates with default state\n- `cascade()` gains a `RenderState` parameter\n- Parser recognizes `:link`, `:visited`, `:hover`; other pseudo-classes are parse errors\n- Specificity: pseudo-class counts as class weight (per CSS 2.1 section 6.4.3)\n- UA stylesheet: `a:link { color: #0000EE }`, `a:visited { color: #551A8B }`, `a:hover { color: #0055EE }`\n- `RenderPipeline::set_hovered_element` + `record_visit`\n- `window.cpp` mouse motion handler + hit-testing\n\n## Privacy limitation (documented)\n\nv1 does not partition `:visited` state per-page. A page can detect visited URLs by rendering links and measuring their color. Real browsers snapshot visited state at page load. Deferred to a future privacy ADR; documented in `current-state.md`.\n\n## Design choices\n\n**Full cascade recompute on state change, not incremental.** Chromium does incremental recomputation with a dependency graph. We do full recompute because:\n\n- Our pages are small (hundreds of nodes)\n- Recomputation is ~1-2ms\n- Correct first, optimize when profiling shows it matters\n\n**Three pseudo-classes, not fifty.** Structural pseudo-classes (`:first-child`) are a separate category (match statically, no state). Logical pseudo-classes (`:not()`, `:is()`) are a third category. Ship one category at a time.\n\n## Deferred\n\n`:active`, `:focus`, `:first-child`, `:nth-child`, `:not()`, `:is()`, Level 4 pseudo-classes, `text-decoration`-based hover, visited persistence to disk, privacy partitioning.\n\n## Implementation plan\n\n~5 commits:\n\n1. `RenderState` + `cascade` overload + `Selector::matches` overload (no behavior change)\n2. Parser extension for the three pseudo-classes + specificity + tests\n3. UA stylesheet rules + tests\n4. `RenderPipeline::set_hovered_element` + `record_visit` + window.cpp mouse handler\n5. Docs refresh\n\nCommits 1-3 make `:link` and `:visited` work without hover. Commit 4 adds hover. Natural intermediate checkpoint after commit 3.\n",
